1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:14,012
Contact Center New-Hire Intelligence is an open-source Databricks accelerator for one difficult operating
question: when does a new-hire cohort become production-ready, and how confident should we be in that
answer?

2
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:26,760
A customer supplies four governed Unity Catalog tables: daily KPI observations, agent assignments,
effective KPI targets, and training classes.

3
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:35,305
A validated configuration generates the canonical Bronze adapter and a reviewable Databricks Asset
Bundle.

4
00:00:35,365 --> 00:00:38,407
Downstream analytics remain unchanged.

5
00:00:39,587 --> 00:00:42,703
The executive page leads with readiness.

6
00:00:42,763 --> 00:00:50,007
It combines target attainment, modeled days to target, process yield, and cohort comparisons.

7
00:00:50,067 --> 00:01:00,348
Filters are associative, so leaders can move from the portfolio view into a specific fictional program,
cohort, KPI, or time window.

8
00:01:01,528 --> 00:01:05,964
A learning curve without production exposure can be misleading.

9
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:12,008
This page places observed and fitted performance beside weekly and cumulative volume.

10
00:01:12,068 --> 00:01:21,784
Four curve families compete for every cohort and KPI, while fit quality prevents weak models from
becoming confident target-date promises.

11
00:01:22,964 --> 00:01:27,694
Driver views compare KPI performance with tenure and handled volume.

12
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:36,586
The fitted series and correlations support investigation, but the product deliberately labels them as
descriptive associations.

13
00:01:36,646 --> 00:01:42,905
That distinction keeps an attractive visual from turning into an unsupported causal claim.

14
00:01:44,085 --> 00:01:55,531
Process-control views add direction-aware one, two, and three sigma limits, first-pass yield, DPMO, and
complementary z-score and IQR outlier methods.

15
00:01:55,591 --> 00:02:02,687
Lower-is-better metrics such as handle time are never ranked as if larger values were better.

16
00:02:03,927 --> 00:02:09,971
Prophet publishes six future planning periods with an eighty percent uncertainty interval.

17
00:02:10,031 --> 00:02:15,874
Databricks Genie uses five governed semantic sources and an executable benchmark suite.

18
00:02:15,934 --> 00:02:25,337
Optional Action Intelligence combines Genie research with retrieved, Git-reviewed playbook content and
persists a reviewable action history.

19
00:02:26,517 --> 00:02:30,774
The workspace is the runtime and presentation surface.

20
00:02:30,834 --> 00:02:33,200
The repository is the product.

21
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:49,344
Lakehouse code, model governance, semantic metadata, dashboard definitions, Genie configuration,
workflows, evaluation, privacy gates, and operating playbooks are version controlled and deployed
together.

22
00:02:49,404 --> 00:02:53,267
Clone it, map your data, validate it, and deploy.
